  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Blur Reveal\n\nA transition: the outgoing scene softens away while the incoming one resolves out of blur, with a faint scale drift.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Two scenes should change with a soft, premium blur dissolve rather than a hard cut or a wipe.\n- The mood is calm, editorial or product-focused.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The change should feel energetic or physical: use a wipe, a whip pan or a glitch cut.\n- You need a transition over the host's own scenes with no panels of its own: copy the filter and opacity logic into the host.\n\nVariables:\n- label_a (string): Panel A title, default \"Before\"\n- sub_a (string): Panel A text, default \"A busy, scattered start.\"\n- label_b (string): Panel B title, default \"After\"\n- sub_b (string): Panel B text, default \"Calm, clear and focused.\"\n- color_a (color): Panel A color, default \"#1d4ed8\"\n- color_b (color): Panel B color, default \"#0f766e\"\n- text_color (color): Text color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 96\n- font (enum): Font, default \"geist\"\n- max_blur (number, 0-80): Max blur, default 24\n- scale_by (number, 0-0.3): Scale drift, default 0.03\n- start_frame (number, 0-300): Transition start, default 30\n- transition_frames (number, 4-90): Transition length, default 22\n- blur_out_exiting (boolean): Blur the outgoing scene, default true\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Blur Reveal\n\n  The outgoing scene softens away while the incoming one resolves out of blur.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui/blob/0aecaca2b61a167992e1205d10e4da16d8a71331/apps/web/registry/bases/default/primitives/blur-reveal.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 RemotionUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"blur-reveal\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"label_a\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel A title\",\n        \"description\": \"Headline of the outgoing panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"Before\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"sub_a\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel A text\",\n        \"description\": \"Supporting line of the outgoing panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"A busy, scattered start.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"label_b\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel B title\",\n        \"description\": \"Headline of the incoming panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"After\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"sub_b\",\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"role\": \"content\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel B text\",\n        \"description\": \"Supporting line of the incoming panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"Calm, clear and focused.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color_a\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel A color\",\n        \"description\": \"Background of the outgoing panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"#1d4ed8\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"color_b\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Panel B color\",\n        \"description\": \"Background of the incoming panel.\",\n        \"default\": \"#0f766e\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"text_color\",\n        \"type\": \"color\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Text color\",\n        \"description\": \"Colour of the panel text.\",\n        \"default\": \"#ffffff\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font_size\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font size\",\n        \"description\": \"Panel headline size in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 96,\n        \"min\": 24,\n        \"max\": 260,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"font\",\n        \"type\": \"enum\",\n        \"role\": \"style\",\n        \"label\": \"Font\",\n        \"description\": \"Typeface.\",\n        \"default\": \"geist\",\n        \"options\": [\n          {\n            \"value\": \"geist\",\n            \"label\": \"Geist\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"poppins\",\n            \"label\": \"Poppins\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"playfair\",\n            \"label\": \"Playfair Display\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"value\": \"grotesk\",\n            \"label\": \"Space Grotesk\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"max_blur\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Max blur\",\n        \"description\": \"Peak blur of a scene in pixels.\",\n        \"default\": 24,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 80,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"px\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scale_by\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Scale drift\",\n        \"description\": \"How far a scene drifts in scale while it blurs.\",\n        \"default\": 0.03,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 0.3,\n        \"step\": 0.005\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"start_frame\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Transition start\",\n        \"description\": \"Frame (30 per second) the transition starts on.\",\n        \"default\": 30,\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 300,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"transition_frames\",\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Transition length\",\n        \"description\": \"Frames the transition lasts.\",\n        \"default\": 22,\n        \"min\": 4,\n        \"max\": 90,\n        \"step\": 1,\n        \"unit\": \"frames\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"blur_out_exiting\",\n        \"type\": \"boolean\",\n        \"role\": \"motion\",\n        \"label\": \"Blur the outgoing scene\",\n        \"description\": \"Off keeps the outgoing scene sharp underneath.\",\n        \"default\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Blur Reveal</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100..900&amp;family=Poppins:wght@400;600;800&amp;family=Playfair+Display:wght@400..900&amp;family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300..700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { color: #f4f4f5; }\n        .brv-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .brv-panel { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.2em; text-align: center; padding: 0 8%; }\n        .brv-bg { position: absolute; inset: -15%; z-index: -1; }\n        .brv-panel { isolation: isolate; }\n        .brv-sub { font-size: 0.34em; opacity: 0.8; font-weight: 500; }\n        .brv-title { font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.05; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"blur-reveal\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"brv-clip\" class=\"brv-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"brv-a\" class=\"brv-panel\"><div class=\"brv-bg\" id=\"brv-bga\"></div><div class=\"brv-title\" id=\"brv-ta\"></div><div class=\"brv-sub\" id=\"brv-sa\"></div></div>\n          <div id=\"brv-b\" class=\"brv-panel\"><div class=\"brv-bg\" id=\"brv-bgb\"></div><div class=\"brv-title\" id=\"brv-tb\"></div><div class=\"brv-sub\" id=\"brv-sb\"></div></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) && v !== \"\" && v !== null ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function bool(v, f) { if (v === undefined || v === null || v === \"\") return f; return !(v === false || v === \"false\" || v === 0 || v === \"0\"); }\n            function pick(v, list, f) { v = String(v); return list.indexOf(v) >= 0 ? v : f; }\n            function clamp01(v) { return v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v; }\n            function lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\n            function ramp(v, a, b, from, to, ease) { var p = b === a ? 1 : clamp01((v - a) / (b - a)); if (ease) p = ease(p); return from + (to - from) * p; }\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n                  var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function mk(tag, parent, cls, text) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (cls) e.className = cls; if (text !== undefined) e.textContent = text; if (parent) parent.appendChild(e); return e; }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            // Every frame is drawn from the frame number alone, so seeking anywhere draws the same frame.\n            function drive(name, frameFn) {\n              var clock = { f: 0 };\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frameFn(clock.f); } }, 0);\n              frameFn(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n            }\n\n            var FONTS = { geist: \"Geist, system-ui, sans-serif\", poppins: \"Poppins, system-ui, sans-serif\", playfair: '\"Playfair Display\", Georgia, serif', grotesk: '\"Space Grotesk\", system-ui, sans-serif' };\n            var fontKey = pick(vars.font, [\"geist\", \"poppins\", \"playfair\", \"grotesk\"], \"geist\");\n            root.style.fontFamily = FONTS[fontKey];\n            var a = document.getElementById(\"brv-a\"), b = document.getElementById(\"brv-b\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-ta\").textContent = str(vars.label_a, \"Before\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-sa\").textContent = str(vars.sub_a, \"A busy, scattered start.\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-tb\").textContent = str(vars.label_b, \"After\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-sb\").textContent = str(vars.sub_b, \"Calm, clear and focused.\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-bga\").style.background = str(vars.color_a, \"#1d4ed8\");\n            document.getElementById(\"brv-bgb\").style.background = str(vars.color_b, \"#0f766e\");\n            var fs = num(vars.font_size, 96, 24, 260) + \"px\";\n            [a, b].forEach(function (p) { p.style.color = str(vars.text_color, \"#ffffff\"); p.style.fontSize = fs; });\n            var maxBlur = num(vars.max_blur, 24, 0, 80), scaleBy = num(vars.scale_by, 0.03, 0, 0.3);\n            var start = num(vars.start_frame, 30, 0, 300), len = num(vars.transition_frames, 22, 4, 90), blurOut = bool(vars.blur_out_exiting, true);\n            var editorial = bez(0.45, 0, 0.55, 1), fadeEase = bez(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n            // presentationProgress 0 to 1: the incoming scene resolves in the last part, the outgoing one leaves in the first.\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var p = editorial(clamp01((frame - start) / len));\n              // Incoming: opacity done 74 % in; outgoing: gone 70 % in. displace is 0 at rest.\n              var inOpacity = fadeEase(clamp01(p / 0.74)), inDisplace = 1 - inOpacity;\n              var outOpacity = 1 - clamp01(p / 0.7), outDisplace = clamp01(p / 0.7);\n              b.style.opacity = String(inOpacity);\n              b.style.filter = inDisplace > 0.002 ? \"blur(\" + (inDisplace * maxBlur).toFixed(2) + \"px)\" : \"\";\n              b.style.transform = \"scale(\" + (1 + inDisplace * scaleBy).toFixed(4) + \")\";\n              if (!blurOut) { a.style.opacity = \"1\"; a.style.filter = \"\"; a.style.transform = \"\"; return; }\n              a.style.opacity = String(p >= 1 ? 0 : outOpacity);\n              a.style.filter = outDisplace > 0.002 ? \"blur(\" + (outDisplace * maxBlur).toFixed(2) + \"px)\" : \"\";\n              a.style.transform = \"scale(\" + (1 - outDisplace * scaleBy * 0.66).toFixed(4) + \")\";\n            }\n            drive(\"blur-reveal\", draw);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
